================================================================================
TEST T33398 -- (260) Management_LLDP - LLDP-Med
================================================================================
Run:      2026-10-21 15:48-16:02 NZDT.  LLDP-MED was measured on the wire on an
          AT-x960-56YSQ, then removed and restored.
          The DUT's clock reads UTC and is 15 s behind the box's UTC.  Device times
          below are UTC, and tool and console times are box local (NZDT).
Bench:    tb277, consoles u2 = swi_d (DUT), u3 = swi_b, u5 = swi_a;
          Test Engineer bidhanc@bidhanc-dl
Tester:   bench-runner
Graded:   tester
Case:     T33398.  The test-case database holds NO authored objective for this case, and
          its single step is an empty placeholder with no description, no test data and
          no expected result.  The only authored authority is the case title.
          The tester designed the objective and all 8 steps below from three sources:
          the case title; the X960 TPS, row 258 "LLDP-Med = Yes"; and the DUT's own CLI
          surface, read read-only with `<cmd> ?` before anything was sent.
          Objective (designed by the tester), in five parts.
          1. The DUT types itself as an LLDP-MED Network Connectivity device, and sends
             no LLDP-MED TLV until an LLDP-MED endpoint appears on the port.
          2. A voice VLAN configured on a port becomes an LLDP-MED Network Policy TLV
             that carries the configured VLAN, priority and DSCP.
          3. The DUT classifies an LLDP-MED endpoint correctly, and a non-MED neighbour
             on the same port differently.
          4. LLDP-MED Fast Start sends the configured number of frames at the fast rate,
             and the trigger for it can be named.
          5. The LLDP-MED configuration can be removed by two different routes, and it
             survives a reboot.
          Every verdict below is graded on frames on the wire.  `show lldp local-info
          med` and `show lldp neighbors detail` are quoted as corroboration only, never
          as the proof.
