VERDICT: PASS -- LLDP-MED works on the AT-x960-56YSQ, and every limb was proven with frames.
      DUT types itself correctly ....... yes      (MED Capabilities TLV: device type=Network Connectivity)
      no MED TLV without an endpoint ... yes      (voice policy fully configured, 40 s capture, 0 MED TLVs on the wire)
      MED TLVs appear for an endpoint .. yes      (4 TLVs -> 7 TLVs when a Class III phone appeared on the port)
      policy carries the configuration . yes      (application=Voice vlan=70 tagged=True priority=5 dscp=46, all as configured)
      two decoders agree ............... yes      (lldpmed_phone.py and lldpwire.py read the same bytes identically)
      endpoint classified correctly .... yes      (Endpoint Class III / Telephone; a plain neighbour on the same port got blank MED columns)
      fast start count and rate ........ yes      (exactly 3 frames at 1.00 s, against a 30.03 s steady state)
      fast start trigger named ......... yes      (it fires when an endpoint is NEW on the port; 4 observations, see STEP 5)
      policy tracks reconfiguration .... yes      (priority 5 -> 6 changed on the wire; VLAN and DSCP did not move)
      removal by TLV deselect .......... yes      (7 TLVs -> 6; MED Capabilities, ordinary LLDP and fast start all still work)
      removal by voice VLAN removal .... yes      (7 TLVs -> 6 by a completely different route; no empty or stale policy sent)
      configuration survives a reboot .. yes      (vlan 70, tagged, non-default priority 6 and dscp 46 all measured after a cold boot)
CAVEAT:  This run proves what swi_d does.  It does NOT prove what swi_a or swi_b believe.
         Both partner consoles were locked out, and neither partner is part of the
         measurement path of this case.
         LLDP-MED Location Identification (`Lo`) was not configured.  The TLV is selected
         by default and reads `[not configured]`.  It is a separate feature with its own
         CLI and needs its own case.
         Extended Power via MDI (`Pe`) is NOT testable on this unit.  The AT-x960-56YSQ
         has no Power over Ethernet and reports `[not supported]` itself.  No bench
         change here could close that.
         `lldp med-notifications`, the LLDP-MED topology change trap, was not exercised
         separately.
         `lldp faststart-count` was not varied.  Its default of 3 was confirmed on the
         wire four times.
         The DHCP phase of the phone emulator was skipped with `--no-dhcp`.  There is no
         DHCP server in VLAN 70 on this bench, so that phase could only have measured the
         bench and not the DUT.
         `switchport voice vlan dot1p`, `untagged` and `dynamic` were read off the CLI
         surface but not exercised.  `dynamic` needs a RADIUS-assigned voice VLAN.
