--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
TOPOLOGY AS TESTED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  LLDP-MED is a point-to-point conversation between the switch and an endpoint on one
  port.  The endpoint in this case is the TESTBOX.  tb277 eth3 emulates an LLDP-MED
  Endpoint Class III IP phone with tools/lldpmed_phone.py, and sends a plain non-MED
  neighbour with tools/lldpsend.py as the control.  Everything is measured on swi_d
  port1.0.10.
  swi_a and swi_b are PASSIVE.  This case never logged in to them and never configured
  them.  They appear only as neighbour rows that the DUT already held on other ports, and
  they are shown here so those rows can be read.

        tb277 eth3   10.38.22.33/27   MAC 00:0d:b9:55:77:0e
        The ACTIVE partner, playing two roles in turn:
          tools/lldpmed_phone.py  -- an LLDP-MED Endpoint Class III IP phone,
                                     chassis / port ID 00:00:5e:00:53:NN, name ck-phone
          tools/lldpsend.py       -- a plain Station-only neighbour, the non-MED control
        It is also the capture point (tcpdump, ether proto 0x88cc)
             |                                    ^
             |  LLDP-MED endpoint advertisements  |  the DUT's LLDPDUs, captured and
             |  into the DUT                      |  decoded on the box
             v                                    |
    +------------------------------------------------------------------+
